    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105777" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρώγλ-η</span></b>  (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῶγλα</span></b> , <u>Gloss.</u>), ἡ,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρώγω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hole formed by gnawing,</i> esp. <i>a mouse's hole,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Batr.
				52
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Babr.
				31.17
			</span></i>: generally, <i>hole,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				552b28
			</span></i>, al.; of a serpent, <i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				4.90
			</span></i>: pl., <i>caves,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>1 Ki.</u>
				14.11
			</span></i>; <i>holes</i> (gnawed) in clothes, <i><span class="en">
				Batr.
				184
			</span></i>; of <i>canals</i> in the flesh, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Carn.</u>
				9
			</span></i>.</div>
